  "id": "Compound::DB00590 - Gene::81033",
  "verbalization": "Doxazosin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Floppy Iris Syndrome, which is mediated through Prazosin. Prazosin, in turn, binds to Kcnh6, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Doxazosin influences Kcnh6. The evidence is consistent across two paths, with both linking Doxazosin to Prazosin, which then binds to Kcnh6. The lowest common ancestors for Doxazosin and Prazosin are both categorized under \"Agent Affecting Cardiovascular System\" and \"Oxacycle,\" indicating a shared biological context. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Prazosin in mediating Doxazosin's effects on Kcnh6, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
